
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
DA = DB [00]
DB = DC [01]
E,A,B are collinear [02]
DE ⟂ AB [03]
BF ⟂ BD [04]
CF ⟂ CD [05]
G,E,D are collinear [06]
G,A,C are collinear [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. DA = DB [00] & DB = DC [01] ⇒  D is the circumcenter of \Delta BAC [08]
002. D is the circumcenter of \Delta BAC [08] & BF ⟂ BD [04] ⇒  ∠FBA = ∠BCA [09]
003. G,E,D are collinear [06] & B,A,E are collinear [02] & DE ⟂ AB [03] ⇒  GE ⟂ EA [10]
004. BF ⟂ BD [04] & GE ⟂ EA [10] ⇒  ∠(FB-EA) = ∠(BD-GE) [11]
005. G,E,D are collinear [06] & G,A,C are collinear [07] & ∠FBA = ∠BCA [09] & ∠(FB-EA) = ∠(BD-GE) [11] & E,A,B are collinear [02] ⇒  ∠BDG = ∠BCG [12]
006. ∠BDG = ∠BCG [12] ⇒  G,C,B,D are concyclic [13]
007. CF ⟂ CD [05] & BF ⟂ BD [04] ⇒  ∠DBF = ∠DCF [14]
008. CF ⟂ CD [05] & BF ⟂ BD [04] ⇒  ∠FCD = ∠DBF [15]
009. ∠DBF = ∠DCF [14] ⇒  F,B,D,C are concyclic [16]
010. G,C,B,D are concyclic [13] & F,B,D,C are concyclic [16] ⇒  G,F,B,D are concyclic [17]
011. G,C,B,D are concyclic [13] & F,B,D,C are concyclic [16] ⇒  G,C,F,D are concyclic [18]
012. G,F,B,D are concyclic [17] ⇒  ∠GFB = ∠GDB [19]
013. G,C,F,D are concyclic [18] ⇒  ∠GFC = ∠GDC [20]
014. G,E,D are collinear [06] & ∠GFB = ∠GDB [19] & ∠FCD = ∠DBF [15] & ∠GFC = ∠GDC [20] ⇒  GF ⟂ GE [21]
015. GF ⟂ GE [21] & GE ⟂ EA [10] ⇒  GF ∥ EA [22]
016. GF ∥ EA [22] & E,A,B are collinear [02] ⇒  FG ∥ AB
